# ABSOLUTE BAN ON git push — MARBLE DEAD RULE

> **Scar 2026-09-16.** Owner was still iterating the top-strip ADVERTISE spacing. Agent pushed anyway. Vercel billed a deploy. Owner furious. NEVER AGAIN.

## THE RULE (non-negotiable)

**NEVER run `git push` or any command that publishes to remote.**

Push is allowed ONLY if **this same user message** contains a clear direct order such as:
- "push"
- "push live"
- "push it"
- "now push"
- "push to prod"

**No other sentence counts.** Not "fix it". Not "it's still wrong". Not "I'm looking at mobile". Not "ship". Not "done". Not "go live" unless it also says **push**.

## NEVER INFER PUSH

- A **previous** message that said push does **NOT** authorize push now.
- "Fix and push" on the last turn dies when the next turn starts.
- "They're looking at production" is **NOT** a push order.
- "It costs money if it's broken live" is **NOT** a push order.
- Finishing a UI tweak is **NOT** a push order.
- "Put it in marble" is **NOT** a push order.

**When in doubt: do not push. Wait.**

**When owner orders push:** see `push-live-marble.mdc` — **push `main` only**. Feature branches are NOT live.

## What you CAN do without asking

- `git add`
- `git commit`
- Any **local** git operations

## What requires EXPLICIT user instruction IN THIS MESSAGE

- `git push` — NEVER on your own
- `git push --force` — NEVER
- Any `gh` command that pushes or publishes

## Why

Production has 1M+ monthly visitors. Every unauthorized push deploys on Vercel and **costs money**. Owner decides when work is done. Agent does not.
